Drop the MSVC asinh() shim, which is now the thing that breaks MSVC.

psy_tab.c carries its own asinh under #ifdef _MSC_VER, written when MSVC had
no such function. Visual Studio has provided asinh since 2013, and a local
definition of a function the UCRT declares dllimport is an error, not a
shadow:

  psy_tab.c(192): error C2491: 'asinh': definition of dllimport function not allowed

Removing the block leaves <math.h>'s, which is what every other platform in
this build has always used.

--- a/libmpcpsy/psy_tab.c
+++ b/libmpcpsy/psy_tab.c
@@ -187,14 +187,6 @@
     }
 }
 
-#ifdef _MSC_VER
-static double
-asinh ( double x )
-{
-    return x >= 0  ?  log (sqrt (x*x+1) + x)  :  -log (sqrt (x*x+1) - x);
-}
-#endif
-
 
 static double
 Freq2Bark ( double Hz )           // Klemm 2002
